2026-10-10 09:21:20,590 INFO 💭 THOUGHT (primary)
DISCUSSION
The bug is that they only check the supplied point lies on the chosen curve over F_p, but they do not check that it has the claimed prime order n. Since scalar multiplication is done over the curve group, I can send a point from a small-order subgroup on the curve (or twist-style invalid subgroup if accepted by the weak check), get Q = dG, recover d modulo that small order, and likely exploit verify by submitting any congruent value if the point order is tiny. First I want to search for an easy way by computing small-order points on the provided curves locally.

